                <pb facs="1637" n="1623" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.24/7–1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reed</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-15">July 15, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1140. Our Embassy in Montevideo reports that a serious situation in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">frigoríficos</hi> may soon result from action of
                    Argentine Government in denying all export permits for shipment of salt to
                    Uruguay. Please report immediately whether there is a shortage of salt in
                    Argentina or whether we should interpret the action of the Argentine Government
                    as an economic sanction against Uruguay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
